 (mori) Mount Hiei across Lake Biwa, or the keepers (yamamori) of nearby Mount Tsuga.","近江八幡市":"Named after Himure Hachiman Shrine. Fukuoka already had a Yahata City in 1954, so the new city added the province name Ōmi. Fukuoka's Yahata later merged into Kitakyūshū, and when Kyoto's Yawata became a city in 1977 no prefix was needed — so the older city carries one and the newer does not."}},"kyu":{"25201":{"t":140,"k":58742,"r":[["Zeze Domain",21377],["@bakufu",13353],["@jisha",12490],["Sano Domain",6410],["@other",5112]]},"25202":{"t":111,"k":62405,"r":[["Hikone Domain",50546],["@bakufu",11715],["@jisha",144]]},"25203":{"t":282,"k":156092,"r":[["Hikone Domain",61112],["@bakufu",39371],["Kōriyama Domain",12195],["Yodo Domain",10837],["@other",32577]]},"25204":{"t":101,"k":58913,"r":[["@bakufu",17255],["@hatamoto",13734],["Kōriyama Domain",12643],["Kawagoe Domain",5922],["@other",9359]]},"25206":{"t":42,"k":29091,"r":[["Zeze Domain",17395],["@hatamoto",4113],["@bakufu",3229],["Yodo Domain",1354],["@other",3000]]},"25207":{"t":53,"k":35109,"r":[["@hatamoto",10787],["Yodo Domain",5736],["@bakufu",5493],["Miyazu Domain",3386],["@other",9707]]},"25208":{"t":40,"k":21795,"r":[["Zeze Domain",6294],["@hatamoto",6260],["@bakufu",3753],["Maebashi Domain",2103],["@other",3385]]},"25209":{"t":119,"k":66269,"r":[["@hatamoto",23079],["Minakuchi Domain",19402],["@bakufu",9135],["Yamakami Domain",3068],["@other",11585]]},"25210":{"t":49,"k":34643,"r":[["@hatamoto",14398],["@bakufu",7611],["Yodo Domain",2512],["Mikami Domain",2363],["@other",7759]]},"25211":{"t":17,"k":11799,"r":[["Yodo Domain",3248],["Minakuchi Domain",2235],["@bakufu",1809],["@hatamoto",1752],["@other",2755]]},"25212":{"t":156,"k":74635,"r":[["Kōriyama Domain",18177],["Ōmizo Domain",17503],["@hatamoto",10864],["@bakufu",7144],["@other",20947]]},"25213":{"t":202,"k":110233,"r":[["@bakufu",59545],["@hatamoto",20988],["Kōriyama Domain",9693],["Hikone Domain",5793],["@other",14214]]},"25214":{"t":92,"k":43935,"r":[["Hi